.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_recursion_memory_management \- obsolete function that does nothing
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_set_recursion_memory_management\fP\f(CR(
      pcre2_match_context *\fP\f(CImcontext\fP\f(CR,
      void *(*\fP\f(CImymalloc\fP\f(CR)(size_t\fP \f(CIsize\fP\f(CR, void *\fP\f(CImydata\fP\f(CR),
      void (*\fP\f(CImyfree\fP\f(CR)(void *\fP\f(CIptr\fP\f(CR, void *\fP\f(CImydata\fP\f(CR),
      void *\fP\f(CImydata\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
From release 10.30 onwards, this function is obsolete and does nothing. The
result is always zero.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.